  ],
  "facts": {
    "start": "created 1956 by France Football (journalists vote); first winner Stanley Matthews (Blackpool), aged 41",
    "rules": "only European players until 1995; worldwide players at European clubs from 1995; anyone from 2007; so Pele and Maradona never won it; France Football's 2016 recount: Pele would have won 7",
    "three": "Cruyff 1971/73/74; Platini 1983/84/85 (three in a row); Van Basten 1988/89/92, last game aged 28 (ankle), retired 1995",
    "ronaldo": "5: 2008, 2013, 2014, 2016, 2017",
    "messi": "8: 2009-2012 four in a row, 2015, 2019, 2021, 2023 (after the 2022 World Cup); 14 years from first to last"
  },
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Who has won the most Ballon d'Ors in history?",
      "scene": {
        "hook": true,
        "bg": "navy",
        "type": "picture",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "picture",
            "image": "ballon_stage",
            "big": "?",
            "bigSize": 420,
            "bigY": 1300,
            "w": 0
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It started in 1956: a French magazine asked journalists to pick Europe's best player.",
      "scene": {
        "bg": "navy",
        "type": "years",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "years",
            "items": [
              {
                "year": "1956",
                "top": "PARIS",
                "label": "The first vote",
                "head": "#d4a017"
              }
            ],
            "w": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "picture",
            "image": "newsroom1956",
            "label": "FRANCE FOOTBALL",
            "w": 8
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The first winner? Stanley Matthews. Aged forty-one.",
      "scene": {
        "bg": "orange",
        "type": "portrait",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "portrait",
            "person": {
              "image": "matthews"
            },
            "name": "STANLEY MATTHEWS",
            "w": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "counter",
            "from": 0,
            "to": 41,
            "word": "YEARS OLD",
            "size": 420,
            "w": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "But for almost forty years, only Europeans could win it. So Pelé and Maradona never did.",
      "scene": {
        "bg": "purple",
        "type": "statement",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "statement",
            "text": "EUROPEANS|ONLY",
            "hi": 1,
            "size": 190,
            "w": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "versus",
            "left": {
              "image": "pele"
            },
            "right": {
              "image": "maradona"
            },
            "leftName": "PELÉ",
            "rightName": "MARADONA",
            "leftNum": "0",
            "rightNum": "0",
            "w": 11
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "In 2016, the magazine went back and recounted. Pelé would have won seven.",
      "scene": {
        "bg": "orange",
        "type": "ledger",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "ledger",
            "title": "RECOUNT",
            "title2": "2016",
            "w": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "portrait",
            "person": {
              "image": "pele"
            },
            "name": "PELÉ",
            "stamp": "7",
            "w": 8
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "So who has won the most? Three legends are tied on three.",
      "scene": {
        "bg": "navy",
        "type": "picture",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "picture",
            "image": "ballon_stage",
            "big": "WHO?",
            "bigSize": 260,
            "w": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "statement",
            "text": "THREE|ON THREE",
            "hi": 1,
            "size": 200,
            "w": 6
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Johan Cruyff, the star of Total Football, who won three European Cups in a row with Ajax.",
